<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:10:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>佩吉·古根海姆的第一家美术馆仅持续了 18 个月。但其21场展览展示了大量现代艺术杰作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/peggy-guggenheims-first-art-gallery-lasted-just-18-months-but-its-21-exhibitions-showed-a-multitude-of-modern-art-masterpieces-180989930/</link><description>伦敦皇家艺术学院举办的一场新展览重访了古根海姆青年美术馆，这座短命的美术馆正是在这里，这位美国社会名流向持怀疑态度的英国公众介绍了超现实主义和抽象主义</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:39:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/peggy-guggenheims-first-art-gallery-lasted-just-18-months-but-its-21-exhibitions-showed-a-multitude-of-modern-art-masterpieces-180989930/</guid></item><item><title>本周抬头即可看到 11 月的海狸满月——未来几个月连续四个超级月亮中的第一个</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/look-up-this-week-to-see-novembers-full-beaver-moon-the-first-of-four-back-to-back-supermoons-over-the-coming-months-180989927/</link><description>下一次发生在平安夜，根据更严格的超级月亮定义，这是自 1787 年以来从未发生过的罕见巧合</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:43:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/look-up-this-week-to-see-novembers-full-beaver-moon-the-first-of-four-back-to-back-supermoons-over-the-coming-months-180989927/</guid></item><item><title>300 年来的欧洲肖像画可以揭示出什么关于不断变化的美容标准？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-can-300-years-of-european-portraits-reveal-about-evolving-beauty-standards-180989931/</link><description>对 486 幅肖像的最新分析表明，理想的腰臀比在 1650 年至 1950 年间有所增加</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:30:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-can-300-years-of-european-portraits-reveal-about-evolving-beauty-standards-180989931/</guid></item><item><title>在玻利维亚新修复的“安第斯山脉西斯廷教堂”内，数百年历史的壁画用安第斯山脉的图像讲述了圣经故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-bolivia-newly-restored-sistine-chapel-of-the-andes-centuries-old-murals-tell-biblical-stories-with-andean-imagery-180989925/</link><description>圣地亚哥德库拉瓦拉德卡兰加斯教堂位于玻利维亚高原海拔近 13,000 英尺处，描绘了《最后的晚餐》中的豚鼠和骑着美洲驼的法师</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:59:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-bolivia-newly-restored-sistine-chapel-of-the-andes-centuries-old-murals-tell-biblical-stories-with-andean-imagery-180989925/</guid></item><item><title>勃起功能障碍药可以减缓阿尔茨海默病吗？临床试验结果显示对某些患者有希望</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-an-erectile-dysfunction-pill-slow-alzheimers-disease-clinical-trial-results-show-promise-for-certain-patients-180989919/</link><description>在服用类似伟哥的药物一年后，没有服用其他痴呆药物的参与者比服用安慰剂的参与者表现出更少的认知下降。但当检查所有服用实验药的个体时，效果消失了</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:26:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-an-erectile-dysfunction-pill-slow-alzheimers-disease-clinical-trial-results-show-promise-for-certain-patients-180989919/</guid></item><item><title>这些濒临灭绝的蛇是北美最美丽的蛇之一。以下是自然资源保护主义者试图拯救它们的方法</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-endangered-snakes-are-some-of-the-most-beautiful-in-north-america-heres-how-conservationists-are-trying-to-save-them-180989916/</link><description>据估计，旧金山袜带蛇的数量不到 2,000 条，它们生活在加州两个县的故乡。因此，专家们正在旧金山动物园饲养一些幼崽，让它们在将这些生物释放到野外之前先行一步。</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-endangered-snakes-are-some-of-the-most-beautiful-in-north-america-heres-how-conservationists-are-trying-to-save-them-180989916/</guid></item><item><title>这座拥有 200 年历史的房屋位于历史悠久的切萨皮克和俄亥俄运河沿岸，曾经被看门人和公园管理员称为家，现在向过夜的客人敞开大门</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/once-called-home-by-lockkeepers-and-park-rangers-this-200-year-old-house-along-the-historic-chesapeake-and-ohio-canal-is-now-opening-its-doors-to-overnight-guests-180989924/</link><description>从 1830 年代到 1920 年代，Lockhouse 8 为几代船闸管理员提供了居住区，他们帮助船只沿着运河航行，这条运河是从大西洋到美国内陆的重要路线</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/once-called-home-by-lockkeepers-and-park-rangers-this-200-year-old-house-along-the-historic-chesapeake-and-ohio-canal-is-now-opening-its-doors-to-overnight-guests-180989924/</guid></item><item><title>希尔玛·阿夫·克林特 (Hilma af Klint) 的一幅极其罕见的抽象画作在拍卖会上以 1,270 万美元的创纪录价格售出。但它到底应该打折吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</link><description>1920 年创作的《Ser III No. 5》以预售估价近 16 倍的价格售出后，批评者指责阿芙·克林特希望将她的“神圣作品”集中保存在一座寺庙中，而不是分散在私人收藏中</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:23:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</guid></item><item><title>这座拥有 2000 年历史的古墓中出土的一个罗马杯子和数百件其他宝藏揭示了古代亚洲帝国丰富的交换网络</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-roman-cup-and-hundreds-other-treasures-unearthed-in-this-2000-year-old-tomb-reveal-the-rich-exchange-network-of-an-ancient-asian-empire-180989920/</link><description>匈奴人统治中亚约300年。现在，在蒙古发现的一座坟墓揭示了田园文化与罗马帝国、汉族和乐浪郡的联系</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:22:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-roman-cup-and-hundreds-other-treasures-unearthed-in-this-2000-year-old-tomb-reveal-the-rich-exchange-network-of-an-ancient-asian-empire-180989920/</guid></item><item><title>伦勃朗的《夜巡》充满生机。研究人员揭示了这件杰作中隐藏的微生物世界</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-night-watch-is-teeming-with-life-researchers-reveal-a-hidden-world-of-microbes-all-over-the-masterpiece-180989917/</link><description>从这幅 17 世纪画作中采集的样本揭示了无数微生物，其中包括 2013 年在日本一家糖厂首次发现的一种令人费解的细菌</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:21:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-night-watch-is-teeming-with-life-researchers-reveal-a-hidden-world-of-microbes-all-over-the-masterpiece-180989917/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家首次目睹巨星吞噬其较小的恒星伴星</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-astronomers-witnessed-a-giant-star-gobble-up-its-smaller-stellar-companion-180989905/</link><description>这次合并在 2025 年底引发了一次喷发，研究人员急忙使用几台地面和太空望远镜记录了这次喷发。利用较旧的数据和计算机模拟的帮助，该团队重建了整个天体物理过程</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:21:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-astronomers-witnessed-a-giant-star-gobble-up-its-smaller-stellar-companion-180989905/</guid></item><item><title>一群孤立的亚马逊狩猎采集者罕见地向外界寻求帮助，引发了对森林退化的担忧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-isolated-group-of-amazonian-hunter-gatherers-made-a-rare-request-for-help-from-outsiders-raising-concerns-about-forest-degradation-180989909/</link><description>大约 20 名土著阿瓦部落成员从雨林中走出来，从邻近村民那里领取食物。该组织几十年来没有与外界联系，因此专家表示，森林砍伐可能使这些人别无选择</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:08:26 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-isolated-group-of-amazonian-hunter-gatherers-made-a-rare-request-for-help-from-outsiders-raising-concerns-about-forest-degradation-180989909/</guid></item><item><title>9 磅重的老鹰似乎在非洲猎杀 60 磅重的狒狒——暗示掠食者也可能追捕我们的祖先</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-pound-eagles-seem-to-be-hunting-60-pound-baboons-in-africa-hinting-the-predators-may-have-gone-after-our-ancestors-too-180989906/</link><description>在乍得东北部，研究人员发现了维罗鹰攻击成年橄榄狒狒的证据，其体重与人类一样重。研究结果表明，早期人类必须提防来自天空的伏击，这可能影响了他们的进化</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-pound-eagles-seem-to-be-hunting-60-pound-baboons-in-africa-hinting-the-predators-may-have-gone-after-our-ancestors-too-180989906/</guid></item><item><title>在中国两个洞穴中发现的牙齿正在改写直立人的故事，直立人是一种远古人类祖先，其能力可能比我们想象的还要强大</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/teeth-discovered-in-two-chinese-caves-are-rewriting-the-story-of-homo-erectus-an-ancient-human-ancestor-that-may-have-been-more-capable-than-we-thought-180989913/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，该物种在亚洲大陆的存在时间比之前认为的要长 216,000 年。另一位研究人员表示，另一种说法是直立人能够生活在热带雨林中，这一发现“颠覆了”常见的灭绝理论。</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:10:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/teeth-discovered-in-two-chinese-caves-are-rewriting-the-story-of-homo-erectus-an-ancient-human-ancestor-that-may-have-been-more-capable-than-we-thought-180989913/</guid></item><item><title>乔治亚·欧姬芙以绘画花卉和沙漠而闻名。为什么我们忘记了她对美国建筑的痴迷？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/georgia-okeeffe-is-famous-for-painting-flowers-and-deserts-why-have-we-forgotten-her-obsession-with-american-architecture-180989911/</link><description>底特律艺术学院举办的新展览展出了近 40 件艺术品，重点展示了艺术家对建筑环境（从乡村农舍到城市摩天大楼）的迷人描绘</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/georgia-okeeffe-is-famous-for-painting-flowers-and-deserts-why-have-we-forgotten-her-obsession-with-american-architecture-180989911/</guid></item><item><title>心爱的河马菲奥娜在吞下不小心扔进动物园围栏的孩子帽子后死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</link><description>动物护理团队最初乐观地认为辛辛那提动物园的网红河马能够自然排出物体并康复，但情况最终变成了“医疗紧急情况”</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:21:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</guid></item><item><title>哈佛归还两个可能属于被奴役者的头骨，150 多年来，这些头骨是从巴西运来用于优生学研究的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</link><description>在研究人员、社区团体和巴西政府多年的压力下，遗骸在里约热内卢和萨尔瓦多举行了隆重的仪式欢迎归来。一个头骨可能属于一位在 1835 年奴隶起义中战斗并死亡的人</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:22:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</guid></item><item><title>观看在英格兰切斯特动物园出生的稀有小犀牛，这是对其脆弱物种的可爱促进</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</link><description>这头小牛出生于 10 月 11 日，健康状况良好，正在与母亲一起探索一个僻静的围场，远离公众视线</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:18:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</guid></item><item><title>美国国立卫生研究院决定明年将最后一批退休研究黑猩猩转移到动物保护区</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</link><description>该机构此前已确定这些动物年龄太大或患病，不适合此次旅行。但最近涉及另一个联邦政府支持的研究机构的转移促使美国国立卫生研究院重新审视这个问题</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家最终拼凑出古希腊最大的谜团之一“帕台农神庙之谜”吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</link><description>几个世纪前，帕台农神庙的东山墙已化为废墟。德国研究人员现在相信，在罗马石棺和 3D 打印机的帮助下，他们已经重现了描绘雅典娜诞生的 39 幅人物场景</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:06:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</guid></item></channel></rss>